<article class="env-lemma" id="0GI1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GI1">Lemma <span data-tag="0GI1">88.25.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$, $W$ be algebraic spaces over $S$ with $X$ locally Noetherian. Let $T \subset |X|$ be a closed subset. Let $a, b : X \to W$ be morphisms of algebraic spaces over $S$ such that $a|_{X \setminus T} = b|_{X \setminus T}$ and such that $a_{/T} = b_{/T}$ as morphisms $X_{/T} \to W$. Then $a = b$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $E$ be the equalizer of $a$ and $b$. Then $E$ is an algebraic space and $E \to X$ is locally of finite type and a monomorphism, see Morphisms of Spaces, Lemma <a href="/tag/03HK" data-tag="03HK">67.4.1</a>. Our assumptions imply we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/0AR6" data-tag="0AR6">88.25.3</a> to the two morphisms $f = \text{id} : X \to X$ and $g : E \to X$ and the closed subset $T$ of $|X|$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>